    },
    {
      "id": "troilus-and-cressida/sceneIV_35.1/p@132336",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "PARIS.\nAnd tell me, noble Diomed, faith, tell me true,\nEven in the soul of sound good-fellowship,\nWho in your thoughts deserves fair Helen best,\nMyself, or Menelaus?",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "troilus-and-cressida/sceneIV_35.1/p@132336/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 6,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "troilus-and-cressida/sceneIV_35.1/p@132336/line-2",
          "start": 7,
          "end": 54,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "troilus-and-cressida/sceneIV_35.1/p@132336/line-3",
          "start": 55,
          "end": 97,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "troilus-and-cressida/sceneIV_35.1/p@132336/line-4",
          "start": 98,
          "end": 144,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "troilus-and-cressida/sceneIV_35.1/p@132336/line-5",
          "start": 145,
          "end": 165,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 6234291,
        "end": 6234501,
        "line": 232157,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap35/p@132336",
        "anchor": "sceneIV_35.1"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "PARIS.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "troilus-and-cressida/sceneIV_35.1/p@132550",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "DIOMEDES.\nBoth alike:\nHe merits well to have her that doth seek her,\nNot making any scruple of her soilure,\nWith such a hell of pain and world of charge;\nAnd you as well to keep her that defend her,\nNot palating the taste of her dishonour,\nWith such a costly loss of wealth and friends.\nHe like a puling cuckold would drink up\nThe lees and dregs of a flat tamed piece;\nYou, like a lecher, out of whorish loins\nAre pleas’d to breed out your inheritors.\nBoth merits pois’d, each weighs nor less nor more,\nBut he as he, the heavier for a whore.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "troilus-and-cressida/sceneIV_35.1/p@132550/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
